  "details": "<p>Sixteen stone altars, all inscribed with inscriptions of the Assyrian king Sargon II (r. 721\u2013705 BC), were discovered in the ruins of the Sebetti\u00a0temple at D\u016br-\u0160arruk\u012bn.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "A temple dedicated to the Sebetti, the divine seven, was excavated by Iraqi archaeologists in 1957. This temple at D\u016br-\u0160arruk\u012bn (modern Khorsabad) is located just west of the citadel, near Citadel Gate A and City Gate 7.",
